  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 204 PM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nNorthwest flow aloft will bring a prolonged period of welcomed dry \nconditions through the weekend and into much of next week. Two upper \nlevel waves are progged to move through the upper Midwest Saturday \nevening and again Wednesday. Taking a look at 1000-500mb RH progs \nfrom latest deterministic model runs, show moisture will be \nquite limited with both waves with a better signal to our north \nfor any light rain. Locally, we will likely end up with just an\nincrease in clouds. Temperatures will be seasonable this \nweekend, with afternoon highs in the mid 60s to low 70s and lows\nin the 40s. A slow warming trend will be seen next week, with \nhighs in the mid 70s by Wednesday. Regarding precip chances, \nensemble model probabilities for QPF > 0.1\" are less than 20% \narea-wide through next weekend. In fact, the latest 6-10 day \nprecip outlook from CPC shows 70-80% combined probabilities of \nnear/below normal precipitation for the Oct 7th-11th time frame.\nIn other words, a dry pattern is in store at least for the next\n10 days allowing ag fields to dry out.",
